WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:11.795
Two hundred and thirty-nine thousand Temporary Foreign Worker positions approved in 2022 alone — up from ninety thousand in 2015, a one hundred and sixty-five percent increase in seven years.

00:00:11.795 --> 00:00:18.522
Eighty-five percent in low-wage categories where Canadian workers were available but employers refused to pay market rates.

00:00:18.522 --> 00:00:22.363
This is not immigration policy — this is a wage-suppression subsidy.

00:00:22.363 --> 00:00:31.499
Workers tied to a single employer, housed in squalor, paid poverty wages, while corporations post record profits and call it a labour shortage.
